            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "> The information is still in the query index, isn't it?\n\nI'm not sure I understand your question. But the document order is never available in the index. It is always calculated.\n\n> What should I do if I have a client that mostly doesn't about document order for most queries, but occasionally would like\n> to use the ordering within the same workspace?\n\nYou would set respectDocumentOrder to true and omit an order by in your query to get document order, otherwise you should add an order by @jcr:score. This effectively disables document order.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mreutegg",
            "name": "mreutegg",
            "key": "mreutegg",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658"
            },
            "displayName": "Marcel Reutegger",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2007-11-27T15:14:59.509+0000",
          "updated": "2007-11-27T15:14:59.509+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12383310/comment/12545901",
          "id": "12545901",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Marcel:\n> I'm not sure I understand your question. But the document order is never available in the index.\n> It is always calculated. \n\nSorry, my (obscured) point was that the query engine is still able to return results in document order even if the default would be to not do that. Unfortunately there is no way for a client to explicitly request that the results should be document-ordered if that's not the default.\n\nBut I guess that's a secondary concern and probably should be addressed with a separate feature request.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2007-11-27T16:30:06.977+0000",
          "updated": "2007-11-27T16:30:06.977+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12383310/comment/12545971",
          "id": "12545971",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=ckiehl",
            "name": "ckiehl",
            "key": "ckiehl",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Christoph Kiehl",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "+1 to change the default for \"respectDocumentOrder\" to \"false\". Most people don't care about document order but about performance and they should get the best performance as possible by default. It's better to let the minority find out how to enable document order than to let the majority find out how to make jackrabbit perform better.\nI think the descriptor should just tell that document order is not supported. Anyone can still enable it for whichever workspaces they like.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=ckiehl",
            "name": "ckiehl",
            "key": "ckiehl",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Christoph Kiehl",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2007-11-27T19:14:11.750+0000",
          "updated": "2007-11-27T19:14:11.750+0000"
        },
        {
